<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · RetroDocs"
  description="Privacy Policy for RetroDocs, the Mac app that opens old Mac and Microsoft Works documents."
  eyebrow="RetroDocs"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  meta="Last updated: October 30, 2026"
  back={{ href: '/apps/retrodocs', label: 'RetroDocs' }}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> RetroDocs collects no data. Your files are opened and converted on your Mac, and nothing is sent to us or anyone else.
  </div>

  <h2>What It Collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The app has no network access, so it cannot upload your files.
  </p>

  <h2>What Stays on Your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your files.</strong> RetroDocs reads only the files and folders you open or drop on it, and writes converted files only where you choose to save them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The one-time unlock is sold through the App Store. Apple handles the payment; we never see your payment details or Apple Account.
  </p>

  <h2>Open-Source Libraries</h2>
  <p>
    RetroDocs includes the open-source libraries libmwaw, libwps and librevenge, used under the MPL-2.0 license. They are listed on the Acknowledgements screen in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Not Affiliated</h2>
  <p>RetroDocs is not affiliated with Apple or Microsoft.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com">matt@mattdonders.com</a></p>
</DocLayout>
